{
  "case": "due2-conditional-duties",
  "source": "Authored for due2; no origin result.",
  "classification": "odrl-core",
  "needs": [],
  "notes": "Authored for due2 as the linearity and exactness regression for decisions/0003 (it was due2-max-mixed before hoisting was withdrawn). One permission carries nine duties, each guarded by its own request parameter (module i enabled) and each with a duty-action refinement read against the witness (pay exactly (4+i).00 EUR, odrl:payAmount, which due2-core binds to the witness source). Guards stay on the duties: W2 evaluates each as `owed` (workflows §5.2), and W3's outstanding set holds the duties that are owed and unfulfilled (§6.1). A positive guard occurrence only lowers the verdict, so unknown guards are uniform variables: k = 0, the two extreme completions decide, and verdict.exact holds in every scenario. Under the withdrawn hoisting the same policy was 512 atoms, and scenario 1 fell back beyond max_mixed to an inexact Indeterminate. The bound itself is exercised by the rebuilt due2-max-mixed.",
